  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/c33000e8aa6c217b5607e43e961aaea10586b615d633dc1b59cc598e2f7af56c.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(x,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(x,2)\\in A\\times B\\,\u2713$\n\n- $(1,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
